      "slug": "tiropita-term",
      "term": "Tiropita",
      "definition": "A Greek cheese pie made with layers of filo pastry and a filling of feta, ricotta and eggs."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": [],
  "criticalTechniques": [],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This tiropita serves 6 and takes 25 minutes to assemble and 40 minutes in the oven. The filling is a simple blend of feta and ricotta bound with eggs, which sets into a firm, sliceable layer between sheets of crisp pastry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Keep unused pastry sheets covered with a damp cloth at all times while you work. Filo dries out within seconds of exposure to air and becomes brittle and impossible to handle. Have the melted butter and pastry brush ready before you open the packet."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 6,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "feta",
              "amount": 400,
              "unit": "g",
