              "groupLabel": "Pastry"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-flour",
              "amount": 200,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "for homemade pastry sheets if filo unavailable",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Pastry note"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oven to 190C. Melt the butter and have the pastry brush ready. Grease the rectangular baking tin with a little melted butter."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In a large bowl, combine the crumbled feta, ricotta and beaten eggs. Mix until the filling is evenly blended. Season with black pepper. Feta is very salty so taste before adding any salt."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Lay a sheet of filo into the tin and brush with melted butter. Repeat with half the remaining sheets, brushing each one. Let the edges overhang the sides of the tin."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour the cheese filling over the pastry base and spread it into an even layer with a spoon or spatula."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fold the overhanging pastry edges up over the filling. Layer the remaining filo sheets on top, brushing each with melted butter. Tuck the top edges down into the sides of the tin."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Score the top lightly into portions. Brush the surface generously with the remaining butter. Bake for 35 to 40 minutes until golden and crisp on top. Rest for 10 minutes before cutting and serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "problem": "The filling is runny after baking",
              "solution": "The eggs need to be fully incorporated. Make sure the filling is well mixed before going in and bake until the centre no longer wobbles."
            },
            {
              "problem": "The pastry top is soggy",
              "solution": "Each sheet must be brushed with butter before the next goes on. Unbuttered layers steam rather than crisp."
            },
            {
              "problem": "The pie is very salty",
              "solution": "Feta varies widely in saltiness by brand. Rinse the feta in cold water and pat dry before use if you find it too strong."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
